 plane learns and chooses routes, labels, memberships and endpoint locations. The data plane is the installed FIB, adjacency, tunnel, label or ASIC/kernel state that moves packets.'),('Route / prefix / next hop','A prefix names a destination range. A route is one candidate path. A next hop is the immediate or recursively resolved forwarding target.'),('RIB / FIB / adjacency','The RIB keeps candidates and selects a route. The FIB is forwarding-ready state. An adjacency is the final neighbor/tunnel/label relationship required to transmit.'),('Recursive next-hop resolution','A BGP or overlay next hop can point to another route, which can recurse again until a connected adjacency or tunnel is found.'),('Route origin / AD / preference','Origin says where a route came from. Administrative distance or Junos route preference chooses between route sources before internal best-path logic.'),('Underlay / overlay','The underlay provides infrastructure transport. VXLAN, EVPN, MPLS VPNs and other service overlays depend on it.'),('VXLAN / VTEP / VNI','VXLAN wraps tenant traffic in UDP/IP. VTEPs encapsulate/decapsulate. L2VNI identifies a bridge domain; L3VNI identifies tenant routing context.'),('EVPN / route types / RD / RT','EVPN uses BGP to signal endpoints and service reachability. RD makes VPN routes unique; RT controls import/export membership.'),('IRB / anycast gateway','IRB combines bridging and routing. Anycast gateway gives the same first-hop identity on multiple fabric nodes. Symmetric IRB commonly carries routed tenant traffic in an L3VNI.'),('BUM','Broadcast, unknown-unicast and multicast traffic requires replication or multicast delivery because there is no one known remote destination.'),('Redistribution / filters / tags','Redistribution re-originates routes between protocols. Prefix filters, communities, route maps and tags preserve policy and prevent feedback.'),('LACP / ESI / DF / multichassis','LACP bundles links. MLAG/vPC/VSX/MC-LAG coordinate chassis. EVPN multihoming identifies the Ethernet Segment with an ESI and elects a DF for selected BUM forwarding.'),('VRF / VLAN / trunk','A VRF is an isolated L3 table, a VLAN is an L2 broadcast domain, and a trunk carries multiple VLANs.'),('ASM / SSM / RPF','ASM lets a receiver ask for a group without naming the source and often uses an RP. SSM names source and group directly. RPF uses the unicast route back toward the source/RP.')]

def e(s): return html.escape(str(s),quote=True)
vendors={}
for x in L: vendors.setdefault(x[0],[]).append(x[1])
primer_html=''.join(f"<div class='term'><h3>{e(a)}</h3><p>{e(b)}</p></div>" for a,b in primer)
matrix=''.join(f"<tr><td>{e(v)}</td><td>{len(ts)}</td><td>{'; '.join(e(t) for t in ts)}</td></tr>" for v,ts in vendors.items())
lessons=''
for i,x in enumerate(L,1):
    v,t,u,cl,fd,pu,me,ve,fl=x
    lessons+=f"""<article class='lesson'><div><span class='badge'>{e(v)}</span><span class='badge'>Fresh 30-day topic</span></div><h2>{i}. {e(v)} — {e(t)}</h2><p><b>Source:</b> <a href='{e(u)}'>{e(u)}</a><br><b>Classification/date:</b> {e(cl)}</p><h3>Beginner foundation — terms you need before this lesson</h3><p>{e(fd)}</p><h3>Problem and why it exists</h3><p>{e(pu)}</p><h3>Control-plane / packet-state story</h3><p>{e(me)}</p><h3>Configuration and evidence teaching</h3><p>{e(ve)}</p><h3>Failure mechanism, prevention, design consequence and reproducible lab</h3><p>{e(fl)}</p><h3>Multivendor / standards implication</h3><p>The durable engineering question is not the vendor command name but the state transition this feature controls. Translate the mechanism into its standards-level role, then find the equivalent control-plane object, RIB/FIB dependency and packet evidence on the other six platforms. Do not assume identical defaults, timers, policy-attachment points or failure actions.</p><div class='figure'><b>Source-linked figure/reference card</b><p>No stable direct vendor-hosted JPG/PNG/WebP was independently verified for this lesson in this run; no image URL is invented.</p><p><b>Source article:</b> <a href='{e(u)}'>{e(u)}</a></p></div></article>"""
srcs=''.join(f"<li><b>{e(x[0])} — {e(x[1])}</b><br><a href='{e(x[2])}'>{e(x[2])}</a><br>{e(x[3])}</li>" for x in L)
css="""*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0;background:#edf3f7;color:#17212b;font:15px/1.62 Arial,sans-serif}.wrap{max-width:1280px;margin:auto;padding:18px}.hero{background:#102a43;color:#fff;padding:30px;border-radius:18px}.card,.lesson,.q,.term,.figure{background:#fff;border:1px solid #d7e1e9;border-radius:13px;padding:18px;margin:14px 0;overflow-wrap:anywhere}h1,h2,h3{line-height:1.25}h3{color:#1d4e6d}a{color:#08679f;word-break:break-word}.grid,.metrics{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(230px,1fr));gap:9px}.metric{background:white;border:1px solid #d7e1e9;border-radius:10px;padding:12px}.metric b{display:block;font-size:21px}.badge{display:inline-block;background:#e7f1f8;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:999px;margin:2px;font-size:12px}table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;background:#fff}th,td{border:1px solid #d7e1e9;padding:8px;vertical-align:top}.figure{background:#fff!important;border-style:dashed}.q label{display:block;margin:7px 0}.feedback{display:none;padding:11px;border-radius:8px}.good{background:#e8f8ed}.bad{background:#fff0f0}button{background:#08679f;color:#fff;border:0;border-radius:7px;padding:8px 12px;margin:5px}.score{font-size:22px;font-weight:bold}@media(max-width:700px){.wrap{padding:7px}table{display:block;overflow:auto}}@media print{body,.card,.lesson,.q,.term,.figure{background:#fff!important}button{display:none}}"""
DOC=f"""<!doctype html><html lang='en'><head><meta charset='utf-8'><meta name='viewport' content='width=device-width,initial-scale=1'><meta name='run-timestamp' content='{TS}'><meta name='lesson-count' content='21'><meta name='beginner-foundation-count' content='21'><meta name='question-count' content='50'><meta name='original-raster-count' content='0'><meta name='fallback-figure-count' content='21'><meta name='30-day-uniqueness' content='PASS'><meta name='question-order' content='Q1-Q50'><meta name='unique-question-fingerprints' content='50/50'><meta name='repeated-stem-templates' content='0'><meta name='repeated-correct-answer-action-patterns' content='0'><meta name='generic-troubleshooting-shells' content='0'><title>Daily Multivendor Routing Lab — {TS}</title><style>{css}</style></head><body><div class='wrap'><section class='hero'><h1>Daily Multivendor Routing Lab</h1><p><b>Run timestamp:</b> {TS}</p><p><b>21 fresh primary lessons · seven vendor groups · exactly 50 ordered questions.</b></p><p>Today's rotation covers OSPFv3 prefix suppression, EIGRP wide metrics, BGP dampening, PIM SSM, OSPF area ranges, BGP-driven SD-WAN route tags, multi-AS BGP neighbor groups, community policy, SR-TE, MLAG reload timing, IGMP snooping querier, FRR SSM/Large Communities/RFC 9234 roles, Junos prefix guards/LFM/LACP periodic negotiation, and AOS-CX MVRP/VSF split detection/passive OSPF.</p></section><section class='card'><nav><a href='#uniq'>30-Day Uniqueness</a> · <a href='#examvalid'>Exam Validation</a> · <a href='#primer'>Primer</a> · <a href='#matrix'>Matrix</a> · <a href='#lessons'>Lessons</a> · <a href='#multi'>Multivendor</a> · <a href='#exam'>Exam</a> · <a href='#sources'>Sources</a></nav></section><section id='uniq' class='card'><h2>30-Day Uniqueness Validation — PASS</h2><div class='metrics'><div class='metric'><b>15</b>prior sent lab messages checked</div><div class='metric'><b>9</b>recent GitHub report entries checked</div><div class='metric'><b>191</b>prior topic/source baseline</div><div class='metric'><b>54</b>candidate mechanisms rejected</div><div class='metric'><b>21</b>fresh accepted lessons</div><div class='metric'><b>0</b>repeated primary topics</div><div class='metric'><b>0</b>repeated primary source URLs</div><div class='metric'><b>0</b>repeated scenario fingerprints</div></div></section><section id='examvalid' class='card'><h2>Exam Uniqueness / Ordering Validation — PASS</h2><div class='metrics'><div class='metric'><b>50/50</b>Unique question fingerprints</div><div class='metric'><b>0</b>Repeated stem templates</div><div class='metric'><b>0</b>Repeated correct-answer action patterns</div><div class='metric'><b>0</b>Generic troubleshooting-shell questions</div><div class='metric'><b>PASS</b>Feature-specific distractors</div><div class='metric'><b>PASS</b>Question order Q1→Q50</div><div class='metric'><b>A13/B13/C12/D12</b>Fixed answer positions</div></div></section><section id='primer' class='card'><h2>Networking Foundations Primer</h2><p><b>Universal dependency chain:</b> originate/learn → policy → advertise/import → protocol candidate → global RIB ownership → recursion → FIB/adjacency/tunnel/label programming → packet delivery → return path.</p><div class='grid'>{primer_html}</div></section><section id='matrix' class='card'><h2>Vendor/topic matrix</h2><table><tr><th>Vendor</th><th>Fresh lessons</th><th>Topics</th></tr>{m